**EXPERIMENT 19: Jenkins and Docker Integration (Windows – FIXED VERSION)**

---

## 🎯 Objective

To integrate Jenkins with Docker to build and run containers successfully.

---

## 🧭 Startup Guide

### Step 0: Start Docker Desktop

* Open Docker Desktop
* Ensure: **Docker is running**

---

### Step 1: Start Jenkins (IMPORTANT)

```bat
cd C:\Program Files\Jenkins
java -jar jenkins.war
```

👉 Run CMD as **Administrator**

---

## ⚙️ Execution Steps

---

### Step 2: Create Project

```bat
cd C:\Users\danis\OneDrive\Desktop
mkdir jenkins-docker
cd jenkins-docker
```

---

### Step 3: Create App.java

```bat
notepad App.java
```

```java
public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello from Jenkins + Docker!");
    }
}
```

---

### Step 4: Create Dockerfile

```bat
notepad Dockerfile
```

```dockerfile
FROM openjdk:17
WORKDIR /app
COPY . /app
RUN javac App.java
CMD ["java", "App"]
```

---

### Step 5: Push to GitHub

```bat
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Docker project"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/Daniishhhhh/jenkins-docker.git
git push -u origin main
```

---

### Step 6: Jenkins Job Setup

* New Item → `docker-job`
* Freestyle Project

👉 Git:

```
https://github.com/Daniishhhhh/jenkins-docker.git
```

👉 Branch:

```
*/main
```

---

### Step 7: Build Step (IMPORTANT FIX)

```bat
echo Checking Docker
docker version

echo Building Image
docker build -t jenkins-docker-app .

echo Running Container
docker run jenkins-docker-app
```

---

### Step 8: Build

* Click **Build Now**

